solubility may differ slightly from published values. This is normal and is due to slight batch-to-batch variations.\nL21: * Room temperature shipping (Stability testing shows this product can be shipped without any cooling measures.)\nL22: ## Preparing Stock Solutions\nL23: ## Biological Activity\nL24: Description  | Ixazomib Citrate (MLN9708) is a prodrug of Ixazomib (MLN2238), which is a selective, orally bioavailable inhibitor of 20S proteasome that inhibits the chymotrypsin-like proteolytic (β5) site with IC50 of 3.4 nM and Ki of 0.93 nM, respectively. Ixazomib (MLN2238) also inhibits caspase-like (β1) and trypsin-like (β2) proteolytic sites with IC50 of 31 nM and 3500 nM, respectively.\nL25: Targets  |\nL26: 20S proteasome β5 site ^{cite3†[1] }\nL27: (Cell-free assay) 20S proteasome β5 site ^{cite3†[1] }\nL28: (Cell-free assay) 20S proteasome β1 site ^{cite3†[1] }\nL29: (Cell-free assay) 20S proteasome β2 site ^{cite3†[1] }\nL30: (Cell-free assay)\nL31: 0.93 nM(Ki) 3.4 nM 31 nM 3500 nM\nL32: ## Protocol (from reference)\nL33: \nL34: ## References\nL35: \nL36:   * https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20160034/\nL37:   * https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21903769/\nL38:   * https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B9780124171503000272\nL39: \nL40:   * https://patents.google.com/patent/WO2016165677A1/en?oq=WO+2016165677\nL41: + Expand\nL42: ## Selleck's Ixazomib Citrate (MLN9708) Has Been Cited by 15 Publications\nL43: High-Throughput Screening of FDA-Approved Drug Library Reveals Ixazomib Is a Broad-Spectrum Antiviral Agent against Arboviruses [ Viruses, June 24, 2022, 1381]  | cite4†PubMed: 35891362†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L44: The novel RNA polymerase I transcription inhibitor PMR-116 exploits a critical therapeutic vulnerability in a broad-spectrum of high MYC malignancies [ bioRxiv, April 21, 2025, nan]  |\nL45: Rational drug combination design in patient-derived avatars reveals effective inhibition of hepatocellular carcinoma with proteasome a